# sm-show.env: settings for the production show_service (docs/SHOW_ENGINE.md), run by scripts/ctl in GNU screen
# session 'sm-show'. Always on (unlike the renderer): it starts with `scripts/ctl start all`.
#
# OWNER: screen-machine-c8 (flags); wiring and the port register: screen-machine-ca.
# SHOW_PORT is the AV-block allocation in docs/PORTS.md: 127.0.0.1 only; pages reach it through :8700/show/*.
# Never put --port in SHOW_ARGS. Any other KEY=VALUE line here is passed to the process as an env var.
# Format: KEY=VALUE per line, read by scripts/ctl (never sourced). After an edit: scripts/ctl restart show.
#
# Senders (VBAN, receiver-initiated: show_service subscribes from WSL and the replies come back through NAT):
#   test-piano: 98's VBAN test piano on this host (tools/show_sender, udp 6981), started on demand.
#   The kiosk sender (room-mic, room-piano) joins once 98's show-sender.service is deployed on the kiosk.
# Art-Net: the P0 "virtual Maestro" feeds room_service's existing receiver on 127.0.0.1:6454 in patch.yaml's layout.
#   It sends nothing while the room is quiet (it stops after 10 s of quiet).
SHOW_PORT=8703
SHOW_ARGS="--sender testpiano=localhost:6981/test-piano --artnet-target 127.0.0.1:6454 --log-level INFO"
PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1
CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=
OMP_NUM_THREADS=1
OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1
